1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:03,199
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,199 --> 00:00:05,279
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,279 --> 00:00:07,159
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:07,159 --> 00:00:09,280
[SNORTS]
This is Mommy Pig.

5
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,479
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,879
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,879
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

8
00:00:13,879 --> 00:00:15,920
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

9
00:00:17,919 --> 00:00:20,279
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

10
00:00:20,279 --> 00:00:24,240
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are helping
Grandpa Pig pick vegetables.

11
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:27,240
Peppa, here is a lettuce.

12
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:29,240
Thank you, Grandpa.

13
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,479
Oh, what's that?

14
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:34,960
Aah! There's a horrible monster
on it.

15
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,199
[SNORTING]

16
00:00:36,199 --> 00:00:37,559
Monster.

17
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:39,400
[BOTH LAUGHING]

18
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,640
That's not a monster.

19
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,480
It's just a little snail.

20
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,360
PEPPA:
Oh, where has he gone?

21
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:51,000
GRANDPA PIG:
He's hiding in his shell.

22
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,800
PEPPA:
Is that where he lives?

23
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,160
GRANDPA PIG:
Yes, it's his house.

24
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:59,000
Look, he's coming out again.

25
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,919
Hello, Mr. Snail.

26
00:01:00,919 --> 00:01:02,239
[LAUGHS]

27
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:05,800
Grandpa, does Mr. Snail
have a bed in his house?

28
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,000
[LAUGHS]

29
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,840
No, Peppa.

30
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:13,280
If I were a snail
I'd have a bed and a table

31
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:17,320
and a chair and a fridge
and a television.

32
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,759
[ALL LAUGHING]

33
00:01:19,759 --> 00:01:22,640
Grandpa, what do snails eat?

34
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:25,960
Well, mostly they eat
my vegetables.

35
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,479
[MUNCHING]

36
00:01:27,479 --> 00:01:29,600
GRANDPA:
Oi, stop that,

37
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,800
you cheeky rascal!

38
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,200
[BOTH LAUGHING]

39
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:37,119
Grandpa, George and I
want to play cheeky snails.

40
00:01:37,119 --> 00:01:38,280
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

41
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:41,720
These baskets
can be your shells.

42
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:45,880
There, now you look
like two cheeky snails.

43
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:47,479
[GIGGLES]

44
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:50,960
I'm going to eat up
all Grandpa Pig's lettuce.

45
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:54,679
Oi, keep off my lovely lettuce,
you cheeky snails.

46
00:01:54,679 --> 00:01:55,960
[BOTH LAUGHING]

47
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,759
And when Grandpa Pig
shouts at me

48
00:01:58,759 --> 00:02:01,679
I'll hide
in my little house.

49
00:02:01,679 --> 00:02:03,119
[GIGGLING]

50
00:02:03,119 --> 00:02:05,199
[ALL LAUGHING]

51
00:02:05,199 --> 00:02:06,919
[BELL RINGING]

52
00:02:06,919 --> 00:02:09,199
All of Peppa's friends
are here.

53
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:11,920
[BLEATING AND BARKING]
[LAUGHING]

54
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,640
Hello, Grandpa Pig.

55
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:15,000
Hello, Suzy.

56
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,359
Have you come to play
with Peppa and George?

57
00:02:18,359 --> 00:02:19,600
Yes.

58
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,840
I don't know where they are.

59
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,200
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE GIGGLING]

60
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:26,480
It's just me
and these two snails here.

61
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:30,880
PEPPA:
We are cheeky snails
We are cheeky snails

62
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,480
[PEPPA AND GEORGE
GIGGLING]

63
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,720
Surprise!

64
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,040
[BOTH SNORTING]

65
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:37,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

66
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:40,840
[SNORTS]
We were pretending to be snails.

67
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,120
[BLEATING]

68
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,600
Can we be snails too?

69
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,359
I don't think I have
enough baskets

70
00:02:46,359 --> 00:02:48,320
for you all.
ALL: Aww!

71
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,440
You could be
something else, though.

72
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,239
Something exciting
from the garden.

73
00:02:53,239 --> 00:02:54,480
A carrot?

74
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,239
Rebecca Rabbit likes carrots.

75
00:02:56,239 --> 00:02:59,679
GRANDPA PIG:
No, Rebecca, not carrots.

76
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,120
Come over here.

77
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,720
[ALL LAUGHING]

78
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,959
[BUZZING]

79
00:03:03,959 --> 00:03:05,959
[SNORTS]
What's that buzzing sound?

80
00:03:05,959 --> 00:03:09,239
It's coming
from that little house.

81
00:03:09,239 --> 00:03:11,760
Grandpa,
why is that doll's house

82
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:13,920
making a funny
buzzing noise?

83
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,840
That's not a doll's house,
Peppa.

84
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,720
It's a bees' house.

85
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:21,200
It's called a hive.

86
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,399
ALL:
Ooh.

87
00:03:22,399 --> 00:03:25,120
Look, here's one now.

88
00:03:26,399 --> 00:03:27,560
[SLURPING]

89
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,239
PEPPA:
What's he doing?

90
00:03:29,239 --> 00:03:32,359
GRANDPA PIG:
She's collecting nectar
from the flower,

91
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:35,239
and then she flies back
to the hive

92
00:03:35,239 --> 00:03:37,280
to make it into honey.

93
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,239
Hmm. I like honey.

94
00:03:39,239 --> 00:03:41,359
Let's pretend to be bees.

95
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:43,600
[BUZZING]

96
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,239
Yes, let's be bees.

97
00:03:46,239 --> 00:03:48,760
[BUZZING]

98
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,959
[LAUGHING]
[ALL BUZZING]

99
00:03:50,959 --> 00:03:54,560
My, what busy bees.

100
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,399
Yes, we're busy bees.

101
00:03:57,399 --> 00:03:58,760
[BUZZING]

102
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:02,119
Now we must fly back to our hive
to make honey.

103
00:04:02,119 --> 00:04:03,679
[ALL BUZZING]

104
00:04:03,679 --> 00:04:05,959
[ALL LAUGHING AND BUZZING]

105
00:04:05,959 --> 00:04:08,320
Goodness me.
What do we have we here?

106
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,519
Granny, we're busy bees.

107
00:04:10,519 --> 00:04:11,839
[BUZZING]

108
00:04:11,839 --> 00:04:14,959
Ah, would you busy bees
like some toast?

109
00:04:14,959 --> 00:04:17,640
ALL: Yes, please!
GRANNY: And what would you like

110
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,680
on your toast?
ALL: Honey!

111
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:22,800
That's lucky,
because that's what I've made.

112
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,159
Toast and honey.

113
00:04:24,159 --> 00:04:25,920
ALL:
Hooray!

114
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,599
I like being a bee,

115
00:04:27,599 --> 00:04:30,479
because they eat
lots of lovely honey.

116
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:32,000
I like being a snail,

117
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,080
because they eat
all Grandpa's lettuce.

118
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,240
[GIGGLES]

119
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,640
Oi!
Oh!

120
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,560
You cheeky rascal.

121
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,159
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

122
00:04:41,159 --> 00:04:43,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

123
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,479
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

124
00:04:51,479 --> 00:04:53,479
NARRATOR:
Today, as a special treat.

125
00:04:53,479 --> 00:04:56,280
Peppa and George are visiting
Daddy Pig's office.

126
00:04:56,280 --> 00:05:00,440
Daddy, what do you do
at your office all day?

127
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:02,000
Lots of fun things.

128
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,320
[SNORTS]
You'll see.

129
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,680
This is the building
where Daddy Pig works.

130
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,880
We're here.

131
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:09,200
PEPPA:
Hooray!

132
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,640
[BOTH LAUGHING]

133
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,880
[BUZZES]
WOMAN [ON INTERCOM]: Yes?

134
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:14,919
Hello. It's Daddy Pig.

135
00:05:14,919 --> 00:05:16,640
Hello, Daddy Pig.

136
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:18,840
[SNORTS]
Can I press the button too?

137
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,080
[LAUGHS]
Of course, Peppa.

138
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,240
[BUZZES] 
Yes?

139
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,360
It's me.
[WOMAN LAUGHS]

140
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,640
WOMAN:
Hello, Me.

141
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,479
Come in. 
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

142
00:05:28,479 --> 00:05:29,960
[ALL LAUGH]

143
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:33,760
My office
is on the top floor.

144
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,520
We have to go up
in the lift.

145
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,359
[SNORTS]
Can I press the button?

146
00:05:37,359 --> 00:05:39,560
I think it's George's turn.

147
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,840
Press the top button,
George.

148
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,320
[LAUGHS]

149
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,599
BOTH:
Ooh.

150
00:05:46,599 --> 00:05:49,840
NARRATOR:
The lift is taking Peppa,
George and Daddy Pig

151
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,280
up to the very top floor.

152
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:54,240
PEPPA AND GEORGE: Wow!
FEMALE VOICE: Top floor.

153
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,560
Doors opening. 
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

154
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,240
[GIGGLES]

155
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:01,240
NARRATOR:
This is Daddy Pig's office.

156
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,400
Hello, everyone.

157
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:05,280
Hello, Daddy Pig.
Hello, Daddy Pig.

158
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:08,120
Mr. Rabbit and Mrs. Cat
work with Daddy Pig.

159
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:11,599
I've brought two very special
visitors with me today:

160
00:06:11,599 --> 00:06:14,280
[SNORTS]
Peppa and George.

161
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,640
What an honor.

162
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,560
Let's begin the tour.

163
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,240
Mr. Rabbit, can we start
at your desk?

164
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,719
We certainly can.

165
00:06:21,719 --> 00:06:23,000
[CLEARS THROAT]

166
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,479
My job is all about numbers.

167
00:06:25,479 --> 00:06:29,039
I take very important
pieces of paper.

168
00:06:29,039 --> 00:06:32,919
I take a rubber stamp
and I stamp the paper.

169
00:06:32,919 --> 00:06:34,159
[THUDDING]

170
00:06:34,159 --> 00:06:35,719
BOTH:
Wow!

171
00:06:35,719 --> 00:06:38,320
What a great job
Mr. Rabbit has.

172
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,039
Can I do some stamping?

173
00:06:40,039 --> 00:06:42,880
Of course.
I'll just find you some paper.

174
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,719
[SNORTS]
Here's some paper.

175
00:06:44,719 --> 00:06:46,159
[THUDDING]
[LAUGHING]

176
00:06:46,159 --> 00:06:49,240
Uh, maybe we should use
some blank paper.

177
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,039
Here you are.

178
00:06:51,039 --> 00:06:53,479
Peppa likes stamping
with rubber stamps.

179
00:06:53,479 --> 00:06:56,359
I like doing
Mr. Rabbit's job.

180
00:06:56,359 --> 00:06:58,840
[THUDDING]
[GEORGE AND PEPPA LAUGHING]

181
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,080
On with the tour.

182
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:03,039
[SNORTS]
Next up is Mrs. Cat's desk.

183
00:07:03,039 --> 00:07:04,280
[MEOWS]

184
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,120
Hello, Peppa and George.

185
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,359
[SNORTS]
Hello.

186
00:07:07,359 --> 00:07:10,200
My job is all about
drawing shapes

187
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,440
on the computer.

188
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,080
[BEEPING]

189
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,599
PEPPA AND GEORGE:
Ooh.

190
00:07:14,599 --> 00:07:17,719
Then I print the shapes out.

191
00:07:17,719 --> 00:07:19,320
[WHIRRING]

192
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,840
PEPPA AND GEORGE:
Wow!

193
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,560
[LAUGHING]

194
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,719
And here's another copy.

195
00:07:24,719 --> 00:07:26,520
[WHIRRING]

196
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,320
Thank you.

197
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:30,840
What a nice job
Mrs. Cat has.

198
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,479
Can I have a go?

199
00:07:32,479 --> 00:07:34,599
Maybe it's George's turn
now.

200
00:07:34,599 --> 00:07:36,080
That's right, George.

201
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,880
It's your turn
to do some work.

202
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,159
[SNORTING]

203
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,760
[LAUGHING]

204
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,680
George is making
blue triangles.

205
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,440
Now we print them out.

206
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,680
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

207
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,159
[WHIRRING]

208
00:07:48,159 --> 00:07:50,359
[PEPPA AND GEORGE LAUGHING]

209
00:07:50,359 --> 00:07:52,560
I like doing
Mrs. Cat's job.

210
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,719
[DADDY PIG LAUGHING]

211
00:07:53,719 --> 00:07:55,640
Do you want
to see my desk now?

212
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:56,880
Yes, please.

213
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,560
[SNORTS]

214
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,400
This is Daddy Pig's desk.

215
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:04,840
My job is quite
complicated.

216
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,719
I take big numbers,
transmute them

217
00:08:07,719 --> 00:08:10,799
and calculate
their load bearing tangents.

218
00:08:10,799 --> 00:08:14,039
Daddy Pig's job
sounds very important.

219
00:08:14,039 --> 00:08:16,359
Do you use rubber stamps?

220
00:08:16,359 --> 00:08:19,200
No.
Do you use a computer?

221
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:23,560
No. But I do use
coloring pens.

222
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:26,400
Daddy, can we draw
with your coloring pens?

223
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,080
Good idea.
[BOTH GIGGLING]

224
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:31,120
Peppa and George love drawing
with coloring pens.

225
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,280
I'm drawing a house.

226
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,679
George is drawing
a dinosaur.

227
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:36,880
[GIGGLES]

228
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,919
George always
draws dinosaurs.

229
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:41,400
Dinosaur.

230
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,280
Grrr!

231
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,520
[BOTH LAUGHING]

232
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,640
[ALARM RINGING]

233
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:49,600
My goodness.
Five o'clock already.

234
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,040
It is home time.

235
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:55,319
I say, what a splendid picture
of a house.

236
00:08:55,319 --> 00:08:57,959
And what a fierce dinosaur.

237
00:08:57,959 --> 00:09:00,880
George and I
have been doing Daddy's job.

238
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:04,160
And they've been doing it
very well.

239
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:06,520
I like doing
Mr. Rabbit's job.

240
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:09,319
And I like doing
Mrs. Cat's job.

241
00:09:09,319 --> 00:09:12,600
But I like doing
Daddy's job the best.

242
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,680
[ALL LAUGH AND SNORT]

243
00:09:17,839 --> 00:09:20,280
[♪♪]

244
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,520
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

245
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,160
[ALL LAUGHING]
NARRATOR: Grandpa Pig is taking

246
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,640
Peppa and her friends
for a day out on his boat.

247
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,439
[SNORTS]
Everyone on board?

248
00:09:29,439 --> 00:09:31,920
ALL:
Aye, aye, Captain Grandpa!

249
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,640
Full sail!

250
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,240
ALL:
See you later!

251
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,880
ALL:
See you later!

252
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,959
[ALL LAUGHING]

253
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:43,560
Peppa and her friends
are all wearing life jackets.

254
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,640
[SNORTS]
George, you could wear

255
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:46,800
my pirate hat.

256
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,199
[SNORTING]
[ALL LAUGHING]

257
00:09:49,199 --> 00:09:53,240
Today, we are sailing
to Pirate Island.

258
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:55,199
ALL:
Ooh.

259
00:09:55,199 --> 00:09:59,199
If we're lucky,
we might find buried treasure.

260
00:09:59,199 --> 00:10:01,120
ALL:
Wow!

261
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:04,000
Pirate Island sounds like
a great place.

262
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,560
Land ahoy!

263
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,800
[ALL LAUGHING]

264
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,079
Here we are.

265
00:10:12,079 --> 00:10:14,319
Pirate Island.

266
00:10:14,319 --> 00:10:16,240
ALL:
Hooray!

267
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,439
What's that?

268
00:10:19,439 --> 00:10:22,439
It's a metal detector.

269
00:10:22,439 --> 00:10:24,560
It finds buried treasure.

270
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,920
ALL:
Ooh!

271
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,640
[BEEPING]

272
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,920
Grandpa Pig is using
the metal detector

273
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:33,240
to find buried treasure.

274
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:35,040
[BEEPING]
Ah-ha!

275
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,319
The metal detector
has found something.

276
00:10:37,319 --> 00:10:39,640
Let's dig it up.

277
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,600
It's a little coin.

278
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,760
Treasure.

279
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:45,640
ALL:
Hooray!

280
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,360
Let's find some more.

281
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,520
[BEEPING]

282
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,720
Ah-ha!
We've found something else.

283
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,719
It sounds big.

284
00:10:53,719 --> 00:10:55,800
[ALL LAUGHING]

285
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,160
My goodness.

286
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:02,880
This piece of treasure
is quite heavy.

287
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,079
Oh, dear.

288
00:11:04,079 --> 00:11:05,680
That is not
buried treasure.

289
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,839
That is a rusty,
old shopping trolley.

290
00:11:07,839 --> 00:11:09,079
Oh.

291
00:11:09,079 --> 00:11:10,400
[ALL LAUGHING]

292
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:12,400
That's enough
treasure hunting.

293
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,199
Who wants to help
build a big sand castle?

294
00:11:15,199 --> 00:11:17,040
ALL:
Me! Me! Me!

295
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:19,520
What a good idea,
Granny Pig.

296
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:22,439
[SNORTS]
I'll just check on the boat.

297
00:11:22,439 --> 00:11:24,680
Granny Pig is going to help
the children

298
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:26,719
build a big sand castle.

299
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:30,360
And Grandpa Pig is doing
important boat things.

300
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,839
Ah, this is nice.

301
00:11:32,839 --> 00:11:34,040
[YAWNS]

302
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,880
Maybe I'll just
close my eyes

303
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,079
for a little bit.

304
00:11:38,079 --> 00:11:40,160
[SNORING AND WHISTLING]

305
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,920
Granny and the children
are making a big sandcastle.

306
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:48,839
They need lots
and lots of sand.

307
00:11:48,839 --> 00:11:51,719
They use buckets
to make the castles turrets.

308
00:11:53,199 --> 00:11:54,920
[LAUGHS]

309
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,400
What a splendid castle.

310
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,839
ALL:
Hooray!

311
00:11:57,839 --> 00:11:59,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

312
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,680
Time to go home.

313
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:04,240
Oh! Where's the boat gone?

314
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,959
PEPPA:
Look, Granny!

315
00:12:05,959 --> 00:12:07,560
[SNORING]

316
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,240
Oh, no. Grandpa Pig
is fast asleep,

317
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:12,600
and the boat
is drifting away.

318
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,839
GRANNY PIG:
We have to wake Grandpa up.

319
00:12:14,839 --> 00:12:16,880
Shout as loudly as you can.

320
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,800
ALL:
Grandpa Pig!

321
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,360
Wake up!

322
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,600
Wake up!

323
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:26,160
Oh, no.
Grandpa Pig is still asleep.

324
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:28,880
Grandpa's too far away
to hear us.

325
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:31,640
[SNORTS]
We're stuck on Pirate Island.

326
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,280
We're castaways.

327
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,480
[BLEATS]

328
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:36,480
We'll be here
for a hundred years.

329
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:40,240
We'll have to eat
wild fruit and berries.

330
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:42,480
[BARKS]
And well have to eat

331
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,160
insects and slugs.

332
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,400
[ALL GRUNT]

333
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,000
[ALL LAUGHING]

334
00:12:49,719 --> 00:12:52,240
The parents are here
to collect the children.

335
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:55,560
[SNORING AND WHISTLING]

336
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:56,760
Where am I?

337
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:58,160
ALL:
Hello!

338
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:00,040
Uh, hello, everyone.

339
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,800
Have you had a nice time?

340
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,280
Yes. Uh...

341
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:06,760
Actually, I just left
something behind.

342
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,160
Back in a tick.

343
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,319
[ENGINE REVVING]

344
00:13:10,319 --> 00:13:11,760
Look.

345
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,040
There's Grandpa.

346
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:14,680
We're saved.

347
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,160
ALL:
Hooray!

348
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,599
Welcome aboard,
me hearties.

349
00:13:18,599 --> 00:13:20,079
Naughty Grandpa Pig.

350
00:13:20,079 --> 00:13:22,160
We thought
you'd left us behind.

351
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:24,439
Sorry about that,
Granny Pig.

352
00:13:24,439 --> 00:13:27,280
Next time I promise
not to fall asleep.

353
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:28,719
[ALL LAUGHING]

354
00:13:31,439 --> 00:13:33,480
Goodbye, Pirate Island.

355
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,880
See you again soon.

356
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,280
[SNORTS]
I love Pirate Island.

357
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,719
Can we visit it again?

358
00:13:39,719 --> 00:13:40,959
[LAUGHS]

359
00:13:40,959 --> 00:13:43,000
Of course we can, Peppa.

360
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,360
ALL:
Hooray!

361
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,439
[ALL LAUGHING]

362
00:13:48,839 --> 00:13:50,560
[♪♪]

363
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,599
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

364
00:13:53,599 --> 00:13:56,199
NARRATOR:
Today it is raining
a little bit.

365
00:13:56,199 --> 00:13:58,240
[BOTH LAUGHING]

366
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,959
Peppa, George,

367
00:14:00,959 --> 00:14:03,000
put your rain clothes on.

368
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,400
When it rains, Peppa and George
must wear their rain clothes.

369
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,640
Yuck!

370
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,079
George does not like
wearing his rain hat.

371
00:14:12,079 --> 00:14:14,640
George, you must
keep your hat on.

372
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,880
Why?

373
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,839
Because you must keep dry.

374
00:14:17,839 --> 00:14:19,000
Why?

375
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,839
Because you might
catch a cold.

376
00:14:20,839 --> 00:14:22,120
Why?

377
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:24,479
George, do you want to play
in the garden?

378
00:14:24,479 --> 00:14:25,680
[SNORTING]

379
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,079
Then keep your hat on.

380
00:14:27,079 --> 00:14:29,120
[SNORTS]
Come on, George!

381
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:32,040
Peppa and George are going
to jump in muddy puddles.

382
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:34,079
[BOTH LAUGHING]

383
00:14:35,439 --> 00:14:36,920
Yuck.

384
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,760
George does not want to wear
his rain hat.

385
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,439
[LAUGHING]

386
00:14:42,319 --> 00:14:44,640
MOMMY PIG:
Peppa! George!

387
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:46,079
Come inside!

388
00:14:46,079 --> 00:14:49,240
The rains too heavy
to play in now.

389
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,360
[SNORTS]
Oh, George.

390
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,800
Where's your hat?

391
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,360
[SNEEZES]

392
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:57,280
George has caught a cold.

393
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:59,079
[SNEEZES]

394
00:15:00,079 --> 00:15:01,839
Oh, poor little George.

395
00:15:01,839 --> 00:15:03,199
You don't sound well.

396
00:15:03,199 --> 00:15:04,319
[COUGHS]

397
00:15:04,319 --> 00:15:05,640
[SNORTS]
Don't worry.

398
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,520
I'll ring
Dr. Brown Bear.

399
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,800
[DIALING]

400
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,880
[RINGING]

401
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:13,400
Dr. Brown Bear speaking.

402
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,599
I see.

403
00:15:14,599 --> 00:15:16,000
Put George to bed

404
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,520
and I'll be straight round.

405
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,479
Thank you,
Dr. Brown Bear.

406
00:15:19,479 --> 00:15:21,079
Goodbye.

407
00:15:21,079 --> 00:15:24,000
Will George be taken
to a hospital

408
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,520
and given medicine?

409
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:28,439
No. George just has
to go to bed.

410
00:15:28,439 --> 00:15:33,040
Oh? So George
is not really, properly ill.

411
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,240
[SNEEZES]

412
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:37,400
Ugh! That's disgusting!

413
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:38,599
[COUGHING]

414
00:15:38,599 --> 00:15:39,880
Poor George.

415
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,560
Let's get you
straight to bed.

416
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,319
[♪♪]

417
00:15:44,839 --> 00:15:47,199
George,
you have to stay in bed

418
00:15:47,199 --> 00:15:48,920
for a bit.
No.

419
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,959
George does not want
to stay in bed.

420
00:15:50,959 --> 00:15:52,160
[SNEEZES]

421
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,120
George, you have
to stay in bed

422
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,359
until you are better.

423
00:15:55,359 --> 00:15:56,560
Why?

424
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,760
Because you have
to keep warm.

425
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,959
Why?

426
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:03,199
Uh...
Because Dr. Brown Bear says so.

427
00:16:03,199 --> 00:16:05,839
Hello. Where's my patient?

428
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:07,439
[GASPS]

429
00:16:07,439 --> 00:16:11,680
Open wide and say, "Ah."

430
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,680
George is a little bit
worried.

431
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:17,319
Hmm. Peppa, you're big
and brave.

432
00:16:17,319 --> 00:16:21,120
Can you show George
how to say, "Ah"?

433
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:23,079
[SNORTS]
Of course.

434
00:16:23,079 --> 00:16:24,479
Ah.

435
00:16:24,479 --> 00:16:25,800
[GIGGLES]

436
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,719
Ah.

437
00:16:27,719 --> 00:16:30,800
Hmm. George has
caught a cold.

438
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,760
Does George need
medicine?

439
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:37,160
No. But he can have
some nice warm milk at bedtime,

440
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,479
to help him sleep.

441
00:16:38,479 --> 00:16:40,040
Thank you,
Dr. Brown Bear.

442
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,280
You're welcome.

443
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,560
Goodbye.

444
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,920
[HORN HONKS]

445
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:49,920
George has been in bed all day.

446
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:52,280
Now it is Peppa's bedtime.

447
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:55,000
George, are you better?

448
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,280
[SNEEZES]

449
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,640
George is not better.

450
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:58,959
[SNEEZES]

451
00:16:58,959 --> 00:17:01,880
George, please don't sneeze
so loudly.

452
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,160
[COUGHING]

453
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,359
[GRUNTS]

454
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:06,200
This is impossible.

455
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,119
George, here's
some nice warm milk,

456
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:10,720
to help you sleep.

457
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,240
[SLURPS]

458
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,839
[YAWNS]

459
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:17,079
The warm milk makes George
feel very, very sleepy.

460
00:17:18,319 --> 00:17:21,159
Good night,
my little piggies.

461
00:17:21,159 --> 00:17:22,319
[YAWNS]

462
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:24,680
It's so nice and quiet.

463
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,720
[GEORGE SNORING LOUDLY]

464
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:33,480
[ROOSTER CROWING] 
It is morning.

465
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:36,720
[SNORING LOUDLY]
George has slept very well.

466
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,240
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

467
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,680
[LAUGHING]

468
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,360
[LAUGHING]
[BED CREAKING]

469
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,639
[YAWNS]

470
00:17:42,639 --> 00:17:43,840
[ROARS]

471
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,080
George is better.

472
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:46,600
[GIGGLING]

473
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:49,320
Come on, everyone.

474
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:52,560
It's a lovely, sunny day.
[SNORTS]

475
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:54,399
George is wearing
his rain hat.

476
00:17:54,399 --> 00:17:56,639
He doesn't want to catch
another cold.

477
00:17:56,639 --> 00:17:57,879
Oh, George.

478
00:17:57,879 --> 00:18:00,000
You don't need
to wear your hat.

479
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,200
Why?

480
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,800
Because it's hot
and sunny.

481
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,159
Why?

482
00:18:04,159 --> 00:18:08,720
George, can you stop
saying "why" all the time?

483
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,960
Why?

484
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,240
[GIGGLING]

485
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,480
[LAUGHS]

486
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,960
George certainly is better.

487
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,800
[ALL LAUGHING]

488
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,879
[LAUGHING]

489
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,280
[♪♪]

490
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:21,600
[GIGGLING AND SNORTING]

491
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,879
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

492
00:18:22,879 --> 00:18:24,800
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

493
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,520
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

494
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,000
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

495
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,760
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

496
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:33,760
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

